============================================================
PART 4: CYCLOTOMIC STRUCTURE
============================================================

  phi satisfies x^2 - x - 1 = 0  → roots: phi, -1/phi
  tau satisfies x^3 - x^2 - x - 1 = 0  → roots: tau, alpha, alpha_bar

  The companion matrices define linear recurrences:
  M_phi = [[1,1],[1,0]]  (Fibonacci matrix)
  M_tau = [[1,1,1],[1,0,0],[0,1,0]]  (tribonacci matrix)

  The "tau-phi clock" = eigenvalues of these matrices on the unit circle:

  Fibonacci eigenvalues: [ 1.61803399 -0.61803399]
    phi = 1.6180339887
    -1/phi = -0.6180339887

  Tribonacci eigenvalues: [ 1.83928676+0.j         -0.41964338+0.60629073j -0.41964338-0.60629073j]
    tau = 1.8392867552
    alpha_1 = -0.4196433776+0.6062907292j  |alpha| = 0.7373527058
    alpha_2 = -0.4196433776-0.6062907292j  |alpha| = 0.7373527058

  The complex tribonacci root alpha:
    alpha = (-0.41964337760708065+0.6062907292071997j)
    |alpha| = 0.7373527058
    arg(alpha) = 124.688997°
    1/|alpha|^2 = 1.8392867552
    |alpha|^2 = 0.5436890127
    Compare: 1/tau = 0.5436890127
    tau * |alpha|^2 = 1.0000000000
    (Should be 1 by Vieta's: product of all 3 roots = 1)

